+topic roots, and TM2c made them move the plan (accept, deny, refuse) and the effective voice. TM3 makes the
+difference show in the whole reply: the colour of the line, the reason given, and what a resident brings up on their
+own. No resident byte, no new RAM on any console. Files: the new grammar file
+`core/data/talk/grammar/en/trait_voice.tlk`, `core/src/talk_traits.c` (`talk_trait_bring_up`, `talk_preview_trace`,
+`talk_trace_trait_voice`), `core/src/talk_dm.c` (the idle chatter), `core/tools/talk_census.c` (`--traits`),
+`core/tests/test_talk_tm3.c`, `core/tests/test_talk_census.c`.
+
+**Voice colour (layer c) and the reason (layer b).** `trait_voice.tlk` is 320 lines in 170 rules: 312 lines under a `trait=`
+guard (13 for each of the 24 traits; no line deleted anywhere, the register is the house's) and 8 idle remarks. For each trait: a greeting (`core.greet.t_*`,
+for people without their own cast voice: `!cast`), a no to an invitation (3) and to a favour (2) (`core.invite.t_*_no`,
+`core.ask_favor.t_*_no`: a reason or a counter-offer in each, lint L5), an opinion they like (`!stance=con`) and one
+they do not (`!stance=pro`) (`core.ask_opinion.t_*`), and the reason clause after a stance answer
+(`reason.t_*_pro / _con`, depth 1, 2 lines each way). The weights are above the plain lines (greeting 14, refusal 16,
+opinion 10, reason 5) so a person with the trait speaks in its voice most of the time and not always. The five edgy
+traits (hot-headed, romantic, snob, jealous, mean) carry `adults_only&!kid_present` on every line (lint L9), `morbid`
+carries `!kid_present`; nothing here is romance, mocks a person or touches grief; a refusal stays a plain no.
+`talk_gen` already read the speaker's room set (`talk_trait_room`), so in a kid room or for a minor the trait guard is
+false anyway (two locks).
+
+**What a resident brings up.** `talk_trait_bring_up(id, aud, seed, &dir)` returns a concept of one of the person's
+liked roots (65%) or of a disliked root (35%, when they have one) that the room may hear and that their stance on it
+really leans that way (`talk_gen_stance`; a like or hate of their own wins over the root and then it is not the root's
+remark). Never romance or safety, never a grief topic, nothing for the pet. The drama manager's idle chatter
+(`DK_IDLE`) uses it: for the "what is on my mind" pick it takes the bring-up topic 60% of the time, and when the
+speaker has no specific like. The line is an `idle.liked` (stance pro) or `idle.disliked` (stance con) remark, four
+lines each: a mild "I'm not a fan of {x}. Carry on." that is never aimed at the player. (The spec's 5.3 said a
+disliked root is never brought up; the TM3 task allows the mild gripe, so it is the one exception.)
+
+**Creator preview.** `talk_preview_trace` is `talk_preview_line` with the generator's trace;
+`talk_trace_trait_voice(trace)` says which trait's guard a line came from (0 none). The preview for two trait sets of
+the same resident and seed gives a different greeting, answer and refusal (below).
+
+**Measured** (`core/build/talk_census --traits`, `talk_census_traits_share`; 1,000 adults with sliders from a hash and
+two trait sets each that share no trait, the same context through `talk_preview`; "before" is the TM2F tip, same
+function):
+
+| lines that differ between two sets | before | after |
+|---|---|---|
+| greeting | 50.1% | 82.4% |
+| answer | 86.0% | 96.0% |
+| refusal | 48.4% | 90.6% |
+| carry a trait's own voice (greeting / answer / refusal) | 0 | 54% / 54% / 81% |
+| hot-headed vs kind refusal, same sliders and seed: lines differ | | 100% (own bank for both 45%) |
+
+The same set always says the same line (1,000 of 1,000). Edgy traits are inert: for a minor the line with a lone
+edgy trait is the line with no trait in 1,440 of 1,440 cases (5 traits x 6 life stages x 3 kinds x 24 seeds), and with
+a child in the room (a child speaker or an adult beside a child) in 1,080 of 1,080, with no edgy voice line picked;
+an adult alone shows it (182 of 360 in the table, 72 of 360 in the room test). Idle chatter: food is the topic of 49%
+of the idle remarks when both talkers like food, 29% when they have no liked root (the speakers' own specific likes
+carry the rest).
+
+Smoke census (20,000 contexts, seed 20261108, `make -C core talk-census` grid): Surface 17,184 -> 17,186 distinct,
+Skeleton 17,086 -> 17,092, Meaning 5,088 -> 5,115, Chao1 Surface 177,129 -> 177,377; conversations 1,000 of 1,000,
+quality failures 0, S3 hits 0. The lines replace plain ones in the same contexts, so a 20,000 context run cannot show
+much more; the 1,000,000 Surface target is still missed and is not this package's (it needs more lines that name the
+topic). **Q8 stays at the TM2F budgets**: Q8a 0 of 515, Q8b 9 of 3,979 (0.23%), Q8c 0, Q8d 0, Q8e 0, Q8f 0.
+
+**Costs.** `TALK_en.BIN` 909,052 -> 924,796 B (+15,744 B, non-resident; the PS1 subset budget note of 6c stands).
+Stack: `gen_line` 2,096 B and `talk_gen_line` 624 B on MIPS, unchanged (no change in `talk_gen.c`);
+`talk_trait_bring_up` 176 B. MIPS `.text`: `talk_traits.o` 15,008 -> 16,304 B, `talk_dm.o` 34,352 -> 34,416 B. GBA: `.iwram`
+11,272, `.iwram_bss` 4,088, `.data` 816, `.bss` 254,836, every overlay equal to the base `e587f9c1` (net zero); ROM
+`.text` +864 B, `.rodata` +15,744 B (the Talk database is in the ROM). PS1: the EXE built with the boot FMV ends 132,608 B
+below the stack top, as before (Talk is not linked on the PS1: 0 B resident; TKP's 12 KB share of
+PARALLEL_WAVES section 3 still counts `talk_traits.o` at 16 KB with the preview, which TKP should keep out of the
+resident set). Dreamcast: host tests green, no `dc/` change.
+
+**Tests** (`test_talk_tm3.c`, 8; `talk_census_traits_share`, 1): the edgy-inert tables (preview and kid room), every
+trait-guarded alternative's guards (edgy ones adults-only and kid-free, at least 13 lines for each of the 24 traits),
+a trait's own line reaches greeting, answer and refusal, the preview differs for two sets, the bring-up (liked root
+first, the stance leans that way, never romance, safety or grief over every resident in an adult and a kid room),
+the idle remarks follow the liked root, and the census share with the hot-headed against the kind.
+Core tests 1,345 -> 1,354.
